  "id": "sportsmanship",
  "term": "sportsmanship",
  "definition": "In organizational psychology, sportsmanship is an employee’s tendency to stay positive and constructive when work conditions are difficult or inconvenient, rather than engaging in excessive complaining or fault-finding. It reflects tolerance of less-than-ideal situations in ways that support a cooperative work environment.",
